    rdf:value """Germantown, Sunday March 6. 04
Came here, after dining in Philadelphia with Uncle William and family. Had supper (a very poor one) with John and Pearlie and their family.
Bernhard was taken by Mr. Lathrop to lunch with Mr. Stanford White, who showed him Mr. Poer’s house. He dines with Mr. Hodder and talked late about Miss Gwinn, whom Hodder vows he is wild to marry.
Germantown, Monday March 7. 04
Shopped and saw oculist. Minnie Kimbre gave me a reception to meet the old members of the “Questant”. I recognized them all. I drove over to Bryn Mawr with John Thomas, dined with Carey, and gave an address which went off all right.
Came back to spend the night at the house of Mamie and tom Morton, such a
pretty real colonial house. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 194 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1903-04> .

